# An inventory for orange-ops, one host per line:
#   <name> <role> <ssh> <p2p> <rpc> [option=value ...]
# p2p is the public address peers dial; rpc a private address (VPC or
# WireGuard) that only the operator's machines, Prometheus and the other
# hosts reach. 192.0.2.0/24 and 10.0.0.0/8 below are placeholders.
#
# An operator lists only their own hosts; key= is the key on the operator's
# machine that `configure` pushes (mode 0600): a validator's consensus key,
# or an observer's node key (`orange key generate --out ...`).
val-a     validator  orange@192.0.2.10    192.0.2.10:30333    10.0.0.10:8545  key=keys/val-a.key
val-b     validator  orange@192.0.2.11    192.0.2.11:30333    10.0.0.11:8545  key=keys/val-b.key
boot-1    bootnode   orange@192.0.2.20    192.0.2.20:30333    10.0.0.20:8545  key=keys/boot-1.key
rpc-1     rpc        orange@192.0.2.30    192.0.2.30:30333    10.0.0.30:8545  key=keys/rpc-1.key history=100000
# A node added later joins from its peers' snapshots, trusting the group key
# the operator's own nodes report:
#rpc-2    rpc        orange@192.0.2.31    192.0.2.31:30333    10.0.0.31:8545  join=sync trust=10.0.0.10:8545,10.0.0.11:8545
